  "interpretation": {
    "hypotheses_for_independent_future_data": [
      "Muskrat diel activity or camera detectability is region/context dependent rather than a stationary transferable species trait.",
      "The strict east holdout also induces source-stratum and targeted-site domain shift, so geographic transfer and sampling-network transfer are entangled.",
      "Future validation should separate spatial extrapolation from survey-network/domain shift and allow predeclared region-varying activity only in a new programme with new response data."
    ],
    "not_supported": [
      "A causal eastward change in muskrat behaviour.",
      "A causal protocol or country effect.",
      "Retuning the E4 activity model, changing thresholds, rerunning E4, or switching backend.",
      "Upgrading the small positive state gain to confirmatory or causal evidence."
    ],
    "supported": [
      "The negative aggregate activity gain is concentrated in deployments with observed muskrat events: 127 of 128 event-bearing deployments favor the activity knockout, while all 605 zero-event deployments have tiny positive activity gains.",
      "The activity failure is dominated by the D-prefixed heldout source stratum, which contains almost all heldout focal events and almost all negative activity-gain magnitude.",
      "Raw diel event rates remain nocturnally elevated in heldout data, but the night/day rate contrast is much weaker than in the training StateAnnotatedCount stream.",
      "The frozen full model extrapolates a strong diurnal activity slope plus spatial/climate activity slopes far outside the training eastness range; posterior-mean plug-in activity at heldout event contexts is much lower than at training event contexts.",
      "The small positive state gain is not spatially ubiquitous: among event-bearing deployments the sign is mixed, and the net positive result is concentrated in a subset of deployments."
    ]
  },
